Search for audio visual rental for art exhibitions and the results split into two unhelpful kinds: thin rental blog posts that read like a generic checklist, and lighting integrator pages built to design permanent systems for museums and architects, not a one night opening. Neither draws the line an exhibition organizer actually needs. What a rental company sets up for the reception itself, sound sized to the room, a microphone for the artist or curator, a screen for a statement or a video piece, is a different job from lighting the artwork on the walls, which is a specialized discipline most AV rental companies, us included, do not offer.

This page is that honest version, built around a vernissage or opening reception, not a running exhibition. [Contact us](/contact/) with your gallery's guest count and layout if you want us to confirm the right package before you book.

